  "title": "100-Year Floodplain: What Homeowners Should Know",
  "summary": "The term “100-year floodplain” refers to an area where, in any given year, there’s a 1% probability that floodwaters will reach or exceed a defined elevation. FEMA uses this classification to draw Flood Insurance Rate Maps (FIRMs), which determine flood zone designations across the country. For homeowners, buyers, and anyone with a federally backed mortgage, […]",
